<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cossus Cornelius Lentulus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Cossus Cornelius Lentulus Gaetulicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cossus Cornelius Lentulus was a Roman aristocrat and general of the reign of Augustus, consul in 1 BCE. As proconsul of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> around 6 CE he defeated the Gaetuli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> peoples of the Saharan fringe who had risen against the client king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-ii">Juba II of Mauretania</a>. For this victory he received triumphal honours and the surname Gaetulicus, which passed to his son.</p></div>
